{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L40-L75","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition.**\n*The [isotope](#def:isotope-knot) relation is an equivalence on\n$\\{\\text{atom-knots with fixed } Z\\}$.*\n\n*Proof.*\n\n- ***Reflexivity:*** *$K \\sim K$ trivially since $w_{q^Z}^{(1)} =\n  w_{q^Z}^{(2)} = w_{q^Z}$ for $K_1 = K_2$.*\n\n- ***Symmetry:*** *$K_1 \\sim K_2$ iff $w_{q^Z}^{(1)} =\n  w_{q^Z}^{(2)}$, which is symmetric in $K_1, K_2$.*\n\n- ***Transitivity:*** *If $w_{q^Z}^{(1)} = w_{q^Z}^{(2)}$ and\n  $w_{q^Z}^{(2)} = w_{q^Z}^{(3)}$, then $w_{q^Z}^{(1)} =\n  w_{q^Z}^{(3)}$ by transitivity of equality in $S_{n(K)}$.*\n\n*The equivalence classes at fixed $Z$ are parametrised by the\nneutron-quark block $w_{\\bar q^N}$ and inter-nucleon connector\n$w_{\\mathrm{inter}}$, giving the standard isotope chart for\nelement $Z$ (e.g. $Z = 6$: ${}^{12}\\mathrm{C}, {}^{13}\\mathrm{C},\n{}^{14}\\mathrm{C}, \\ldots$).  $\\square$*\n\n**Quotient structure.**\n*The quotient $\\{\\text{atom-knots}\\}/{\\sim}$ at fixed $Z$ is the\n**element class** for $Z$.  This recovers the chemical element\nconcept categorically — element = isotope class.*\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:isotope-knot-equivalence","label":"prop:isotope-knot-equivalence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/isotope-knot-equivalence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_transitivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_transitivity","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (transitivity):\n`K₁ ∼ K₂ → K₂ ∼ K₃ → K₁ ∼ K₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (symmetry): `K₁ ∼ K₂ → K₂ ∼ K₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_reflexivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.claim_reflexivity","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (reflexivity): `K ∼ K` for every atom-knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.isotope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.isotope","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L29-L29","doc":"The isotope relation `∼` on atom-knots at fixed `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.AtomKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.AtomKnot","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L27-L27","doc":"The atom-knot type at fixed `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.N","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L25-L25","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.Z","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L23-L23","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.EquivalenceContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IsotopeKnot/equivalence.lean#L17-L38","doc":"Abstract context for the `equivalence` claim — manuscript-themed\ntyped fields below; the three equivalence-relation laws are\ncaptured as reflexivity / symmetry / transitivity sub-claims on\nthe atom-knot type at fixed `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}